* "German Quad", channel 2, stage 2 of 2: V2A, the V2B cathode follower, the CH2 tone stack and VOLUME 2. Driven by node h (VH2) of the
* channel's first netlist. See preamp.net for the drawing and the assumptions.

V VRAIL x 100 400
R R86 x dp 10k
C C87 dp 0 15u
S VH2 h 1 0

* V2A (shared by the four channels: the relays ST1 and ST3 / ST4 bring the selected channel to h): 470k into the grid, 120k plate, 680R with 2u2; the V2B cathode follower
* (120k, the 10n + 100k load) and 220n into the stacks' input t0 with its 1M.
R R470H h gA 470k
T V2A gA p2 k2 12AX7
R R120B dp p2 120k
R R680A k2 0 680
C C2U2 k2 0 2.2u
T V2B p2 dp kf 12AX7
R R120C kf 0 120k
C C10NF kf c10 10n
R R100KF c10 0 100k
C C220N kf t0 220n
R R1MT t0 0 1M

* CH2 tone stack: R 10k from t0, then 560p and 39k to the treble pot (220k-B) and the node u; two 22n; BASS (1M-A) and MIDDLE (22k-A) rheostats; R 180k into VOLUME 2.
R R10K t0 t 10k
C C560P t tt 560p
R R39K t u 39k
C C22A u bt 22n
C C22B u mt 22n
R VRT_T tt wt 1
R VRT_B wt bt 1
R VRBS bt mt 1
R VRMD mt 0 1
R R180K wt v1 180k
R VRV_T v1 o2 1
R VRV_B o2 0 1
